{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall know this day, etc.</b> Meaning: the test of knowledge required of you this day — that is, after all the signs, etc., that he mentioned in the preceding passage, which justify clear knowledge. And the verse's saying <b>for not et your children</b>, etc., means: the reason I say ״you shall know״ to you specifically, is to say, and not your children — for they do not have knowledge of this test as you do. And there was no need to specify what that knowledge is, for when a person attains understanding through a correct test, the truth appears self-evident to him: that HaShem our Elohim is One, who created everything, rules over everything, rejects those who transgress the Torah, and chooses those who choose it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:26.404257354Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}